# SSH Notebook — Go + Charm conventions

This app serves a Markdown notebook over SSH. SSH is an app-delivery protocol, not a shell — never spawn a shell for the user.

## SSH server (Wish)
- Use `wish.WithMiddleware(...)`; order matters (outermost runs last). Include `logging` and `recover` middleware.
- Persist the Ed25519 host key to disk/secret; never regenerate on each boot (breaks client pinning).
- Auth: password (bcrypt-hashed, from secret) **or** a whitelist of SSH public-key fingerprints. Store per-session identity + permissions in the SSH context.
- Public routes are read-only and sandboxed to the `public/` subtree — never allow edit actions on a public/anonymous session.

## TUI (Bubble Tea)
- One `tea.Model` per SSH session via the `bubbletea` middleware. Keep the standard `Init/Update/View` shape.
- Model is a pure state machine: no blocking I/O in `Update`; do file/git work in `tea.Cmd`s returning messages.
- Handle `tea.WindowSizeMsg` for responsive layout; support small terminals.
- Render Markdown with Glamour; scroll with `bubbles/viewport`. Edit with `bubbles/textarea`.
- Style only with Lip Gloss; no hardcoded ANSI escapes.

## Content & backup
- The notebook is plain files on a Fly persistent volume — the single writer. Access files through an `io/fs`-style abstraction, not raw paths scattered in the TUI.
- Save = write the file to disk. Do NOT put git/network work on the save path.
- Backup is a separate background worker doing a **one-way** push (server → GitHub/object storage), debounced after edits. Never pull onto the volume; never `git push --force`.
- Sanitize paths so a session can never read/write outside the notebook root.

## General
- Use `log/slog` for structured logging; recover from panics per-session so one session can't crash the server.
- Keep packages under `internal/`: `server`, `auth`, `tui`, `content`, `backup`.
- Secrets (password hash, deploy key/PAT) come from env/secret manager — never commit them.
